From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 14:38:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] mlang: know the charset names Windows knows, and answer
 IMultiLanguage from the MIME database.

xmllite asks the MultiLanguage object Word gives it for the code page of
an encoding it does not know itself, and Wine's did not know latin1,
ISO_8859-1, UTF-16 and more than a hundred other names Windows does.
tools/charsetprobe asked Windows 11 about the 158 names of its MIME
database and 33 others:

- IMultiLanguage2::GetCharsetInfo knows 174 of them, with a family code
  page and a code page of its own for each (latin1 is 28591, euc-kr
  51949, gb18030 54936), and names each back as its table has it
  (ibm852 is IBM852, UTF-16 is utf-16).  Wine now has the same table and
  gives the same answers for all 191.
- IMultiLanguage::GetCharsetInfo, older, takes the code pages from the
  MIME database in the registry instead (latin1 is an alias of its
  iso-8859-1, which is code page 1252, and UTF-16 is not there), and
  names them as IMultiLanguage2 does.  It does that now too, and the
  database has x-user-defined, as Windows' has.

Twenty answers of IMultiLanguage's are not the database's either (the
Arabic aliases are 1256 there, csISOLatin5 is iso-8859-5's, CN-GB is
unknown) and are not copied.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 9443b55fb09c0469f92cf7000121973b6094335e)

